Alex,

Thanks for the info.

SciCom can be run inside a ruby REPL, be it the IRB or Pry.  So, the idea is just to let users download their packages on demand the same way it works in R and probably the Renjin REPL.

SciCom dependency is only Renjin which is distributed with it.  I´m now getting ready to release a new version with Renjin 0.8 and would like to allow dynamic downloading of packages.  The current version of SciCom allows dynamic package downloading, but it does not check all the versions the way Renjin is now implementing it, so I will drop my code and use yours.

Thanks again.....

Rodrigo

